    "feedSummary": "One week before Election Day, the Scaling Laws Roadshow visited Emory Law for a conversation with Stacey Abrams, former Minority Leader of the Georgia House of Representatives, bestselling author, entrepreneur, and producer. She joined Kevin Frazier, Director of the AI Innovation and Law Program at the University of Texas School of Law and Senior Editor at Lawfare, and Alex Bores, New York Assemblymember and co-founder of Who Decides. The three explored Leader Abrams’s frameworks for rebuilding democratic power, her efforts to connect people with opportunities to participate, and the role AI might play in those efforts. Leader Abrams also provided an overview of the Ten Steps Campaign, which you can check out here: https://10stepscampaign.org/ Big thanks to Dean Freer, Professor Sag, Matt Winston, and Nadia Hedayat for making the visit possible.",
    "doomIndexInputSummary": "Live from Emory Law: Stacey Abrams joins Alex Bores & Kevin Frazier. One week before Election Day, the Scaling Laws Roadshow visited Emory Law for a conversation with Stacey Abrams, former Minority Leader of the Georgia House of Representatives, bestselling author, entrepreneur, and producer. She joined Kevin Frazier, Director of the AI Innovation and Law Program at the University of Texas School of Law and Senior Editor at Lawfare, and Alex Bores, New York Assemblymember and co-founder of Who Decides. The three explored Leader Abrams’s frameworks for rebuilding democratic power, her efforts to connect people with opportunities to participate, and the role AI might play in those efforts. Leader Abrams also provided an overview of the Ten Steps Campaign, which you can check out here: https://10stepscampaign.org/ Big thanks to Dean Freer, Professor Sag, Matt Winston, and Nadia Hedayat for making the visit possible."
